00:27:12.390 --> 00:27:14.989
But you could conceivably
do that at any location

00:27:14.989 --> 00:27:16.280
that you might want to explore.

00:27:16.280 --> 00:27:17.400
CHAD JENNINGS: Let me
speak specifically.

00:27:17.400 --> 00:27:18.930
If there are people
watching who are

00:27:18.930 --> 00:27:22.990
either in retail, or in
television or radio ratings,

00:27:22.990 --> 00:27:26.490
then these queries are
very readily extensible

00:27:26.490 --> 00:27:31.920
to census tracts,
census blocks, or DMAs.

00:27:31.920 --> 00:27:35.670
So we didn't go to that
extent because we just wanted

00:27:35.670 --> 00:27:37.260
to keep things simple here.

00:27:37.260 --> 00:27:39.720
But if that's your
industry, then

00:27:39.720 --> 00:27:41.050
use those as your template.

00:27:41.050 --> 00:27:42.930
And you can do these
analyses and show them

00:27:42.930 --> 00:27:44.505
on BigQuery Geo Viz.

00:27:44.505 --> 00:27:45.380
SOLEIL KELLEY: Great.

